<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch PM Kok hopes for positive EU effort from Blair.</title>
<headline>Dutch PM Kok hopes for positive EU effort from Blair.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Prime Minister Wim Kok on Friday congratulated Tony Blair on the Labour Party's landslide win in the British general election and said he hoped the new government would be cooperative in Europe.</p>
<p>&quot;Prime Minister Wim Kok today congratulated Labour leader Tony Blair in a telegram and expressed the hope that the new British government will contribute to a positive result at the Intergovernmental Conference in Amsterdam in June,&quot; a government press statement said.</p>
<p>Kok also sent a telegram to Conservative leader John Major thanking him for his cooperation in the past years.</p>
</text>
